.TH "difi" "1" "2026-06-27"
.PP
.SH NAME
.PP
difi - review and refine Git diffs before you push
.PP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\fBdifi\fR [options] [\fItarget\fR]
.PP
\fBdifi\fR < \fIpatch\fR
\fBgit diff\fR | \fBdifi\fR
\fBjj diff --git\fR | \fBdifi\fR
.PP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBdifi\fR is a terminal UI for reviewing diffs from Git, Mercurial, or raw
patch files.\& It opens a two-pane interface: a file tree on the left and a
syntax-highlighted diff view on the right.\& Navigation, commands, and
configuration follow vim conventions.\&
.PP
Run \fBdifi\fR in any repository to review uncommitted changes against a
target branch, commit, or tag.\& You can also pipe raw diff output directly
into \fBdifi\fR from \fBgit diff\fR, \fBjj diff --git\fR, or a patch file.\&
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fB-v, --version\fR
.RS 4
Show version and exit.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB-p, --plain\fR
.RS 4
Print a plain list of changed files and exit (no TUI).\&
.PP
.RE
\fB-f, --flat\fR
.RS 4
Use one-line file navigation in the tree pane instead of
a collapsible directory tree.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB--vcs\fR \fIstring\fR
.RS 4
Force a specific VCS backend.\& Supported values: \fIgit\fR, \fIhg\fR.\&
By default, \fBdifi\fR auto-detects the VCS from the current
directory.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH USAGE
.PP
.SS Invocation
.PP
\fBdifi\fR
.RS 4
Diff against HEAD (or tip for Mercurial).\& This is the most
common invocation.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBdifi\fR \fImain\fR
.RS 4
Diff against the \fImain\fR branch.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBdifi\fR \fIHEAD\(ti3\fR
.RS 4
Diff against 3 commits ago.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBdifi\fR \fI< changes.\&patch\fR
.RS 4
Review a saved patch file from stdin.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBgit diff | difi\fR
.RS 4
Pipe raw Git diff output into \fBdifi\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBjj diff --git | difi\fR
.RS 4
Review Jujutsu changes through \fBdifi\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
.SS Panes
.PP
The screen has two panes: the file tree (left) and the diff view (right).\&
Press \fITab\fR to toggle focus between them, or \fIh\fR and \fIl\fR to focus the
left or right pane directly.\&
.PP
